[19.859529, "o", "\u001b[?25l\r\u001b[4d\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[m I created a new Claude box called \u001b[38;5;153;1mdev-2\u001b[m and checked its weekly quota with \u001b[38;5;153m/usage\u001b[m.\r\n\n  \u001b[1mThe box:\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;153mdev-2\u001b[m is a settings copy of \u001b[38;5;153mdev\u001b[m. It runs Claude Code v2.1.318 with Opus 5.5, signs in with the \u001b[38;5;153mleogr\u001b[m account,\r\n  and shares \u001b[38;5;153mdev\u001b[m's host workdir at \u001b[38;5;153m/var/tmp/showcase/work/yoloctl\u001b[m. It's running with no prompt submitted, and I closed\r\n  the usage panel afterwards.\r\n\n  \u001b[1mWeekly quota:\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n  ┌───────────────────────────┬──────┬─────────────────┐\r\n  │           Limit           │ Used │     Resets      │\r\n  ├───────────────────────────┼──────┼─────────────────┤\u001b[K\r\n  │ Current week (all models) │ 37%  │ Nov 10, 8am UTC │\r\n  ├───────────────────────────┼──────┼─────────────────┤\r\n  │ Current week (Fable)      │ 33%  │ Nov 10, 8am UTC │\r\n  └───────────────────────────┴──────┴─────────────────┘\u001b[K\r\n\n  These limits belong to the \u001b[38;5;153mleogr\u001b[m account, not to the box. The new box has used nothing yet, so these percentages\r\n  mostly reflect usage from \u001b[38;5;153mdev\u001b[m and \u001b[38;5;153mcoordinator\u001b[m, which use the same account.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  To open the new box: \u001b[38;5;153myoloctl box attach dev-2 --space showcase\u001b[m\u001b[29;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[19.859529, "o", "\u001b7\u001b[32;113H\u001b[0;1;30;43m ▸▸ 8x \u001b8"]
